Question ------   Table: Employee

+-------------+------+
| Column Name | Type |
+-------------+------+
| id          | int  |
| salary      | int  |
+-------------+------+
id is the primary key (column with unique values) for this table.
Each row of this table contains information about the salary of an employee.
 

Write a solution to find the second highest distinct salary from the Employee table. If there is no second highest salary, return null (return None in Pandas).

The result format is in the following example.

 

Example 1:

Input: 
Employee table:
+----+--------+
| id | salary |
+----+--------+
| 1  | 100    |
| 2  | 200    |
| 3  | 300    |
+----+--------+
Output: 
+---------------------+
| SecondHighestSalary |
+---------------------+
| 200                 |
+---------------------+
Example 2:

Input: 
Employee table:
+----+--------+
| id | salary |
+----+--------+
| 1  | 100    |
+----+--------+
Output: 
+---------------------+
| SecondHighestSalary |
+---------------------+
| null                |
+---------------------+






Solution ----------   select (
                      select distinct salary
                      from employee 
                      order by salary desc
                      limit 1 offset 1
                      )as secondhighestsalary;






Explanation -------   So We Have An Employee Table Wherein We Have Employee Id & Salary. Here The Question Clearly Asks Us To Find The Second Highest Distinct Salary 
                      From The Employee Table And Tells Us That In Case If We Don't Have Any Second Highest Salary Then We Have To Report It As Null . 

                      The Word Here "Distinct" Means That We Don't Have Any Duplicates Or Repeats And Only The Unique Distinct Values In Our Data As Far As In 
                      This Question We Need Distinct Salary i,e, If There Are Salaries In Our Data Let's Say 100 , 200 , 300 , 300 , 300 , 500 Then The Distinct 
                      Salary Would Mean Only The Unique Values Not The Repeated Duplicate Ones So It Will Be 100 , 200 , 300 , 500 As In Our Example . As We Can
                      Notice In Our Question That We Already Have Distinct Salaries & No Duplicates We Have 100 , 200 , 300 & According To This The Second Highest
                      Salary Would Be 200 . 

                     Now Let's Talk About Our Query . 

                     First We Need To Find The Second Highest Distinct Salary So We Write [ select distinct salary  from employee ] Which Means It Will Only Select 
                     Unique Values In Salary Coloumn From The Employees Table . Now We Write [ order by salary desc ] Which Means That The Data Should Be Ordered As 
                     Per Salary As In Highest To Lowest Which In Our Case Would Look Like --- 300 , 200 , 100 From The Employee Table . Now We Further Write [ limi 1 
                     offset 1 ] Which Basically Means Choose 1 After Leaving 1 Row Which In Our Case Would Mean Leaving 300 & Choosing The Only & Only Value After 300
                     Which Is 200 Which Is Exactly What Our Question Asked - "" The Second Highest Distinct Salary "". After Writing This Whole Query We Select All This 
                     In Bracket & We Write [ Select ---- As Second Highest Salary ] Beacuse As We Have Got Our Final Answer Which Is 200 But We Want To Also Name To Our
                     Table Heading So We Wrote This Query . 
